  The "corresponding source" for a work in object code means all the
source code needed to produce, install, and (for an executable work)
update the work, and to perform all the activities that the user is
permitted to do with the work through its interface.

  The permission to propagate a covered work in object code form is
conditioned on your making available the corresponding source under
the terms of this License.

  "Corresponding Source" for a work in binary form means the source code
for all modules it contains, plus any associated interface definition
files, plus the scripts used to control compilation and installation of
the executable or binary work.

  The Corresponding Source need not include anything that users
can regenerate from other parts of the Corresponding Source.

  The Corresponding Source for a work in object code form must be
the Corresponding Source for the work in binary form.

